WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:54.930
<b>Enter: Captain Usopp</b>

38
00:01:56.930 --> 00:02:00.640
There's absolutely no way we'll make
it to the Grand Line in this condition.

39
00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.020
[LUFFY, ZORO] Huh?

40
00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.770
You're right, we're gonna need
a whole lot more meat.

41
00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:10.440
[LUFFY] Eating fruit
every day is for the birds.

42
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.940
We'll also need
some booze. [grunts]

43
00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.110
[NAMI] Shut up,
you boneheads! Ugh!

44
00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:17.740
That's not what I mean.

45
00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.620
The Grand Line's a dangerous place

46
00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.000
we'll need more than beer
and meat to survive there.

47
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.920
Not to mention the place
is crawling with pirates

48
00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.880
who are also in search
of the One Piece,

49
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:28.210
and they all have ships
that are way better than this.

50
00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:29.590
And we don't have a crew.

51
00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.260
[NAMI] We don't have a crew,
we don't have any equipment,

52
00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:33.930
or even a real ship
for that matter!

53
00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:36.640
There is no way
we'll ever make it like this.

54
00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.260
Yep, we'll need a cook and maybe
a musician to keep us entertained.

55
00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.890
A musician? [laughs]

56
00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:46.230
[NAMI] So... stupid.

57
00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:50.530
A little to the south of here is
an island with some settlements on it.

58
00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.300
And it looks like we might be
able to get our ship

59
00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:53.820
and some of the supplies
we need there.

60
00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.860
Fresh meat at last!

61
00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.240
And lots of booze, as well!

62
00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.000
[USOPP] Sound the alarm!

63
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:03.960
They're here!

64
00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.290
They're here and they're
gonna kill us all!

65
00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.790
Oh, no!

66
00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.090
Pirates! Pirates!

67
00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:12.050
Pirates are attacking!

68
00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.670
Run!

69
00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.630
Everybody run for your lives!

70
00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.970
Pirates! Pirates!

71
00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:19.600
Everybody run!

72
00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.100
Pirates are coming!

73
00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.140
Their bloodlust is unquenchable!

74
00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.100
Uh... we're doomed!

75
00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.570
[USOPP] The pirates...

76
00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:33.110
are a...

77
00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:37.360
<b>Usopp
A Village Youngster</b>

78
00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:34.740
Lie!

79
00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.950
[laughing]

80
00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.700
[USOPP grunts]

81
00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.240
[USOPP] That hurt!

82
00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:44.370
You little liar! You're not
gonna get away this time!

83
00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.080
Wait, wait, wait!

84
00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.000
Now, run!

85
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.090
[yelling continues]

86
00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:57.260
[USOPP laughing]

87
00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:00.510
[USOPP] Just try
and catch me!

88
00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:03.100
– C'mon, slowpokes! [laughs]
– [VILLAGERS yelling]

89
00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.270
Aw, man! Looks
like he got away again!

90
00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.520
That kid's a no good troublemaker!

91
00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.650
He'd better hope
I never get a hold of him!

92
00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:17.490
Looks like nobody's getting
a hold of him today. Hmph.

93
00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:22.330
[USOPP giggles]

94
00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.660
Ah! Yet another job well done!

95
00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.040
It is my solemn duty to send

96
00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.210
the wind of excitement
through this boring, old village.

97
00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.090
[PEPPER] There he is!

98
00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:35.800
[USOPP] Hm?

99
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.220
Hey, you guys!
What's going on?!

100
00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.050
[PEPPER] I bid you
good morning, Captain Usopp!

101
00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:43.430
Fear not! Your loyal crew,
the Usopp Pirates, have arrived!

102
00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.430
<b>Carrot and Pepper
Village Boys</b>

103
00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:45.560
[USOPP grunts]

104
00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.180
Pepper, Carrot. It's just
you two? Where's Onion?

105
00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.600
Have you seen him
around today?

106
00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.690
[ONION screaming]

107
00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:53.860
[ALL] Hm?

108
00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.110
[ONION] Sound the alarm!

109
00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:57.400
They're here! They're here!

110
00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.530
They're here and they're gonna
kill us all! Oh, no!

111
00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:01.780
Hey, it's Onion.

112
00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:03.870
I wonder what
he's freaking out about.

113
00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.330
Pirates! Pirates are here!

114
00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:09.830
<b>Onion
A Village Boy</b>

115
00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.540
Run for your lives! Pirates!

116
00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.250
We don't stand a chance!

117
00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.750
Bloodthirsty murderers have
landed! Run, everybody, run!

118
00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:12.710
[USOPP] Huh?

119
00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.750
Stop playing.

120
00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:17.840
[ONION panting] I'm
not playing!

121
00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.090
[USOPP] Eh... It's for real?

122
00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.260
Yes, it's for real!
Pirates are here!

123
00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:24.260
Gah! Gotta go!

124
00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:26.180
Um... time for me
to have my snack!

125
00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.310
[KIDS] You chicken!

126
00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.480
[USOPP] Actually,
I'm sick! Yeah!

127
00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:34.730
I have, "I'll-die-if-I-
don't-eat-my-snackiosis".

128
00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:36.820
[PEPPER, ONION] You liar!

129
00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:39.440
You always told us that you
wanted to become real pirate

130
00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.150
someday, and now's
our chance!

131
00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.200
[PEPPER] Yeah!
What's with you?

132
00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.910
What kind of a pirate is
afraid of other pirates?!

133
00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:48.160
If I recall correctly, it was
Buggy the Clown's mark.

134
00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.420
[USOPP] B...
Buggy the Clown?

135
00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:56.000
[USOPP] Uh...
I think I'll just...

136
00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.710
But I only saw two tiny boats!

137
00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:02.800
And there were
just three people.

138
00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.930
It's go time,
Brave Usopp Pirates!

139
00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:08.220
We do have a village
to protect!

140
00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.930
Let's go, men! Move out!

141
00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.140
[KIDS] Uh...

142
00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.440
[KIDS] Uh... Sir!

143
00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.530
[LUFFY] Ahh!

144
00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:22.900
[ZORO grunts]

145
00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.360
Feels good to be
on dry land again!

146
00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.240
[LUFFY] There's a village
somewhere around here, right?

147
00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:31.160
[NAMI] Yeah... It looks
like small one, though.

148
00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.120
[LUFFY] Ooh! Ooh!
Then, there's meat!

149
00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.250
There's meat!

150
00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:36.330
There has to be a place
to eat meat in this village!

151
00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.840
Just forget about meat
for a minute, would ya?

152
00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:41.050
[rustling]

153
00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:43.800
[ZORO] Careful...
we're being watched.

154
00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:46.970
Huh? By who? Where
are they? They got meat?

155
00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:47.600
Look out!

156
00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:51.390
[LUFFY yelping]

157
00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:03.070
[LUFFY] Ohh! That's so cool!

158
00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.690
Is this supposed to be
when we're impressed?

159
00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:06.200
[USOPP laughing] I am Usopp!

160
00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.700
Leader of the invincible nation
of pirates who reign over this island!

161
00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:13.290
You stand before a living legend,
the most revered pirate who ever lived!

162
00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.750
I am the Great Captain Usopp!

163
00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:16.960
[LUFFY] Ahh!

164
00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:17.830
[LUFFY] Hm?

165
00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:21.340
Surely you know that plotting an attack
on this island would mean certain death!

166
00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:26.550
My army of eighty million super-mean
pirate soldiers would squash you like bugs!

167
00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:29.550
Awesome!

168
00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:30.350
[NAMI sighs]

169
00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:33.930
[NAMI] You expect
us to believe that?

170
00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.980
Ah! She knows!

171
00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:38.690
Yep! Well, now I know.

172
00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.020
How could I have
been so dumb?!

173
00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.650
I practically told her
I was lying!

174
00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:42.780
I am such an idiot!

175
00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:43.690
So stupid!

176
00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:45.240
[NAMI] Uhh...

177
00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.240
What?! He was lying?!

178
00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.700
[USOPP] Curse you,
you crafty tactician!

179
00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.450
Eighty million may have been
an exaggeration,

180
00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.120
but I have a great many men
under my control!

181
00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:01.210
[KIDS whimper]

182
00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.800
My guess is three.

183
00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:07.550
[KIDS screaming] She
does know!

184
00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.970
[screaming continues]

185
00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:11.970
Hey! Where're you guys
going? Come back!

186
00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:19.270
[laughing] That's pretty cool!

187
00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:21.900
Shut your mouth
or I'll shut it for you!

188
00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.730
I'm a proud man
and I won't stand for it!

189
00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:28.740
This is your last warning,
or you'll get to see why they call me...

190
00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:33.120
"Proud Usopp",
and not "Pushover Usopp".

191
00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.080
Is that clear?

192
00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:38.540
You've already seen for yourself just
how good I am with this thing, so,

193
00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:41.170
you know I could rival
anyone carrying a pistol!

194
00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:50.800
Now that you've drawn your pistol,
are you willing... to use it?

195
00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.260
[USOPP gasps]

196
00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.310
Guns aren't for threats,
they're for actions.

197
00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.390
Are you willing
to risk your life?

198
00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:01.560
[LUFFY] Guns aren't
for threats, they're for actions.

199
00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:10.860
Are you willing
to risk your life?

200
00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.410
[ZORO chuckles]

201
00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.120
Gah. Real pirates definitely
have a lot more punch

202
00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.710
behind their words, 'cause
they can actually back 'em up!

203
00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:21.620
That's so cool...

204
00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.630
I stole that!

205
00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:29.760
[USOPP] Huh?

206
00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:33.210
[LUFFY] I stole those words from
Red Haired Shanks, a pirate I know.

207
00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:34.570
What?

208
00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:37.240
You know Red Haired Shanks?
You really are a real pirate!

209
00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:40.060
Wait, you gotta be lying,
do you really know him?

210
00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:42.350
Yep! I know your dad too.

211
00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.690
[USOPP] Huh?

212
00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.150
His name's Yasopp, right?

213
00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:49.690
[USOPP laughs, yelps]

214
00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.700
[LUFFY chuckles]

215
00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:54.280
[USOPP] Uh... You're right.

216
00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.080
My old man's name is Yasopp.

217
00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:59.750
But, how?

218
00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:01.790
How in the world
do you know him?

219
00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:06.340
<b>Village Diner</b>

220
00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.800
[USOPP] This is good, huh?

221
00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:16.850
So, I met your dad
when I was just a little kid.

222
00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:19.350
Hold on, does my old man
really know Shanks?

223
00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:22.350
Know him?! When I met your dad
he was a part of Shanks's crew,

224
00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.440
so they were probably
pretty good friends.

225
00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:25.560
I can't believe it!

226
00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:29.940
My old man, sailing
the high seas with famous pirates.

227
00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:33.320
[LUFFY] I haven't heard from him
in a while, but I'll bet he's still with them.

228
00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.320
He was a heck
of a sharpshooter!

229
00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.280
I'd keep him on my crew!

230
00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:56.640
Whoa! Good shot!

231
00:10:56.640 --> 00:11:01.140
Eh, that's nothing, I could shoot an ant
between the eyes from across town!

232
00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:04.770
[PIRATES chattering]

233
00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.350
[YASOPP] Ah! You know
something, Luffy?

234
00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:11.230
I got a kid named Usopp,
and he's just about your age!

235
00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:12.740
You told me
about him already.

236
00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:13.740
A hundred times.

237
00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:15.030
A hundred?

238
00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:16.700
[LUFFY grunts]

239
00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.370
Well, too bad!

240
00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:20.660
I'm tellin' ya again!

241
00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:23.200
It broke my heart to leave.

242
00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.250
But I had to go.
You see, Luffy?

243
00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:29.630
When the pirate flag beckons,
you must heed it's call!

244
00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:34.220
[PIRATES cheer]

245
00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:38.300
[LUFFY grunting]

246
00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.390
He used to go on and on
and on about his son.

247
00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:45.060
I think I heard enough about you
to make my ears bleed!

248
00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:47.270
And lemme tell you,
he was a great pirate!

249
00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.060
Yeah? Really?

250
00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.110
I sure am proud
of my old man.

251
00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:55.070
He leapt into a pirate's life
on the endless sea.

252
00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:58.110
And chose a life
of real adventure!

253
00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.370
Maybe you can help us!

254
00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:03.450
Do you know someone who could
provide us with a decent ship;

255
00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.750
or even anyone who knows
how to sail for that matter?

256
00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:09.670
[USOPP sighs] Well, it's
a pretty small village...

257
00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.590
Sorry, but I just don't think
we'll be able to help you.

258
00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:14.170
[ZORO] What about that huge mansion?

259
00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:16.340
The one on top
of that hill over there.

260
00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.050
[USOPP] Ee!

261
00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:19.340
Hey! Do you know
them, Usopp?

262
00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:22.220
With all that money, surely
they could help us get our boat.

263
00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:23.760
You stay away from there!

264
00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:24.770
[NAMI, LUFFY, ZORO] Huh?

265
00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:26.100
Gah! Uh...

266
00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:29.560
I just remembered something
that I really gotta do!

267
00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:35.070
Everybody knows me at this place. So,
uh, stay and eat as much as you want!

268
00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:37.530
Well, uh, gotta go!

269
00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.450
Why was he in such a hurry
to get outta here?

270
00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:48.290
Are you sure this is
the place they took him?

271
00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:50.290
Yeah, those terrible pirates
dragged him inside

272
00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:51.960
and now it's up to us
to save our captain!

273
00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.210
But, guys, those're
real pirates!

274
00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.000
What if they've grilled
and eaten him already?

275
00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:55.500
You idiot!

276
00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.090
It's grisly old witch hags who
eat their victims, not pirates!

277
00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:01.720
This is gonna be the most brutal
and epic battle of our lives,

278
00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:04.010
we must show no mercy
because they will never show it to us!

279
00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:04.850
[KIDS] Hm!

280
00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:09.310
[KIDS] The Usopp pirates,
have arrived!

281
00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:10.720
Who're these kids?

282
00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:12.560
Captain Usopp is gone!

283
00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:13.650
Did they...

284
00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:15.820
Fess up, you filthy pirates!

285
00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:17.570
What have you done
with our beloved Captain?!

286
00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:18.650
Tell us now!

287
00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.280
[ONION, CARROT] Yeah!
Tell us now!

288
00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:23.570
[LUFFY sighs] That meat
sure was good!

289
00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:24.450
– [KIDS gasp]
– What meat?

290
00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.700
These pirates are cannibals!

291
00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:27.660
[giggles]

292
00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.660
What have you done,
you savages?

293
00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:33.130
[ZORO] If you're looking
for your captain...

294
00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:36.090
we ate him.

295
00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.550
[KIDS] Wah! Cannibals!

296
00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:42.760
What are you punks
looking at me for?!

297
00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.720
[LUFFY, ZORO laughing]

298
00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:47.640
[NAMI] You just had to say
something stupid, didn't you?!

299
00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:56.980
<b>Village Mansion</b>

300
00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:00.860
[KLAHADORE] You wish
to see Usopp...

301
00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:03.860
Don't start this, again.

302
00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:06.490
<b>Kaya
Mansion Owner</b>

303
00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:04.990
May I see him?

304
00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.490
I like talking to him.

305
00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:11.790
<b>Klahadore
Mansion Butler</b>

306
00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.240
[sighs] No, ma'am.

307
00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.120
That man is, without a doubt,
a chronic liar.

308
00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:14.290
For someone in your weakened state,

309
00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:17.460
Usopp's outlandish stories
might be too much to handle.

310
00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:20.210
Your late parents instructed
me to protect you to the fullest

311
00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:18.880
But I...

312
00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:25.220
of my abilities. It would be against their
wishes for you to see him, Miss Kaya.

313
00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:28.560
Now then, I'll leave
your medicine right here.

314
00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:30.140
Please be sure to take it.

315
00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:35.900
Killjoy...

316
00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.440
[KLAHADORE] "Killjoy" will do.

317
00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:40.030
A name I'll bear,
if you are kept safe.

318
00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:44.910
– [KAYA whimpers]
– [doors clatter]

319
00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.620
Usopp! You came!

320
00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:54.960
Of course! How are you?
You seem a little down.

321
00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:56.500
[KAYA] I guess I am.

322
00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.880
I'm tired of talking like this, I'd like
to invite inside like a proper guest,

323
00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:04.010
but there's just no way
Klahadore would ever allow that.

324
00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:05.760
He's not a bad person, though.

325
00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:07.180
Don't sweat it!

326
00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:10.680
Remember, I'm a brave warrior of the sea,
who likes endless oceans and the open sky!

327
00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:12.850
Houses weren't made
for rogues like me.

328
00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:15.440
I'd probably just feel
cramped in there. [laughs]

329
00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:18.440
So, what adventure are you
going to tell me about today?

330
00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:21.190
[USOPP] Hmm.
Well, let's see...

331
00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:22.480
Oh, I know!

332
00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.700
What about the story of me
fighting a giant goldfish

333
00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:26.910
at the south pole, when I was
only five years old!

334
00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:27.990
[KAYA] A goldfish?

335
00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:29.830
[USOPP] A giant goldfish!

336
00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:32.830
What first astounded me was
the immense size of it's poop!

337
00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:36.370
It was so big that when I landed
on it, I thought it was solid ground.

338
00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:37.920
It looked like an island!

339
00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:44.920
[USOPP, KAYA laughing]

340
00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:55.140
[LUFFY] Whoa!
This place is huge!

341
00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:57.140
And If our captain
ran off at this hour,

342
00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.980
then this is the place
he's gonna be.

343
00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:01.770
Oh... What in the world
does Usopp come here for?

344
00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.230
He comes to lie.

345
00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:05.030
To lie? That's terrible!

346
00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:06.200
[PEPPER] He's not a bad guy!

347
00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:07.780
He's great! Isn't he?

348
00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:09.530
Yeah! He's awesome!

349
00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:11.410
How is a liar awesome?

350
00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:15.040
[PEPPER] Well, Kaya,
the girl who lives there,

351
00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:17.330
has been in a terrible
depression that's kept

352
00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.830
her weak and in bed
since her parents got sick

353
00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.840
and died a year ago.

354
00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:26.630
She's very rich, but all that money couldn't
help her recover from her sadness.

355
00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:30.930
[ONION] So our captain tells his special made-up
stories to make her laugh and cheer her up!

356
00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:34.060
[CARROT] Captain Usopp is
the best at telling lies!

357
00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:39.480
Wow, that really is
pretty nice of him.

358
00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:40.560
[KIDS] Yeah!

359
00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:44.320
The best thing about him is his mischievous side,
he's always up to something!

360
00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:46.940
I like him 'cause he's not
afraid to be silly!

361
00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:49.400
And I like the Captain's crazy lies!

362
00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:52.410
So when he tells her those stories,
he makes her feel better?

363
00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:54.030
[CARROT] Yep! Lots better!

364
00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:58.330
[LUFFY] Great! I think
we should ask her for a ship after all!

365
00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:00.460
[ONION] Getting
in is impossible!

366
00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:02.750
Those guards at the gate
don't let anyone through!

367
00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:05.050
– [ALL] Uhh...
– [CARROT] Where's Luffy?

368
00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:06.590
– I'll go ask her!
– [ALL gasp]

369
00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:08.380
[ZORO] No!
You're not gonna...

370
00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:14.760
Pardon the intrusion...

371
00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.060
[ZORO] N... No, no, no, no!

372
00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:20.140
– [LUFFY] Rocket!
– [ALL yelling]

373
00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:23.230
[USOPP] So after that terrifying
and traumatic little incident,

374
00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:28.530
we escaped into the sky riding
on a giant slingshot ball!

375
00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:29.820
What's that?

376
00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:30.990
[USOPP] Hm? Uh...

377
00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:32.860
Yahoo!

378
00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:34.660
[yelling]

379
00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:41.080
[LUFFY] That worked well...

380
00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.290
My goodness, are you okay?

381
00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:46.590
Uh... Don't mind them Kaya,
this happens to me all the time.

382
00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:48.510
That's just the price of being
a famous adventurer!

383
00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:52.380
They're just new recruits who heard about me
and came to join the Usopp pirates!

384
00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:55.140
Nope, not me.
I came here to see you.

385
00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:56.930
I wanted to ask you a favor.

386
00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.560
A favor? From me?

387
00:17:58.560 --> 00:17:59.390
[LUFFY] Uh-huh.

388
00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:00.930
I was wondering
if there was any way

389
00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:03.980
– you could help us get a boat.
– [KLAHADORE] You there!

390
00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:06.110
What do you think
you're doing?

391
00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:10.900
Klahadore...

392
00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.240
Get out!

393
00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:16.530
I'll have you know that this is
criminal trespassing.

394
00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:17.530
[USOPP gasps]

395
00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.540
these people are

396
00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:24.210
Not now, Kaya.

397
00:18:24.210 --> 00:18:27.840
You can tell me all about this
riff-raff after they've left.

398
00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:29.840
Now get out! All of you.

399
00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:32.670
Leave now, unless you have
some business with me.

400
00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:36.010
Alright! Do you think that
you could help us get a ship?

401
00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:37.640
[KLAHADORE] Certainly not!

402
00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:38.470
[LUFFY] Aww...

403
00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:39.470
[KLAHADORE] Usopp!

404
00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.270
[USOPP] Crap!

405
00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:43.060
[KLAHADORE] You have
quite the reputation.

406
00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:45.100
You are very well known
in the village.

407
00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:48.320
Quite impressive
for someone as young as you.

408
00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:51.360
Usually, people who admire
me so much, call me Captain.

409
00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.360
So, it's Captain Usopp to you!

410
00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:56.780
[KLAHADORE] Your father also
had something of a reputation.

411
00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.030
What?

412
00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:01.370
You'll never be anything more
than the son of a filthy pirate.

413
00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:05.170
Who knows what sort
of trouble you're up to now?

414
00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:10.550
All I ask is that you and your kind leave
this respectable young lady alone.

415
00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:13.050
A filthy pirate?!

416
00:19:13.050 --> 00:19:16.840
[KLAHADORE] You and she are
from completely different worlds and you know it!

417
00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:19.260
Is it money you're after?
How much do you want?

418
00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.220
Cease this at once, Klahadore!

419
00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:23.270
Apologize to him!

420
00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:25.020
Hey, calm down, Kaya.

421
00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:29.480
I don't believe there is any reason
to apologize to this savage young man, My Lady.

422
00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:30.360
[USOPP gasps]

423
00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:32.400
[KLAHADORE] My goal
isn't to slander.

424
00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.190
I am merely stating the truth.

425
00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:36.610
I sympathize
with your situation.

426
00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:39.120
You must hate your
great, idiot of a father

427
00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:42.910
for abandoning his family and his village
because of his mindless lust for treasure!

428
00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:44.790
Klahadore, stop!

429
00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:48.040
Don't you dare insult
my father ever again!

430
00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:52.090
– [USOPP grunts]
– [KAYA gasps] Usopp!

431
00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:53.090
[KAYA gasps]

432
00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:55.420
[USOPP grunts]

433
00:19:56.970 --> 00:19:59.850
[USOPP growls]

434
00:19:59.850 --> 00:20:02.390
Why have you gotten
so worked up, Usopp?

435
00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:05.310
It's times like these when you
should do what you do best and lie.

436
00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.770
Tell me about how your father
is really a traveling salesman,

437
00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:11.310
or about how you aren't
really related by blood.

438
00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:12.860
[USOPP] Enough!

439
00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:15.400
[KAYA gasps]

440
00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:16.780
[ALL gasp]

441
00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:22.620
[USOPP growls]

442
00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:24.120
[KIDS] Captain!

443
00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:27.250
[KLAHADORE grunts] Case in point.

444
00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:28.540
He resorts to violence!

445
00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:31.460
I guess the apple never falls
far from the tree, does it?

446
00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:33.460
Shut up!

447
00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:37.090
My father listened to his heart
and chose a life of risk and adventure!

448
00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:40.550
I am proud to say that my old man
is a brave warrior of the sea!

449
00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:43.600
You're right, I have been known
to exaggerate from time to time,

450
00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:46.140
but I will never lie
about who my father is!

451
00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:49.100
I refuse to be ashamed
of my heritage!

452
00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:51.480
I am the son of a pirate!

453
00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:55.610
[PEPPER, ONION whimper]

454
00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:57.490
Captain...

455
00:20:57.490 --> 00:21:01.280
[KLAHADORE laughs] Pirates
are brave warriors of the sea,

456
00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:03.660
are they? [laughing]

457
00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:06.830
That's quite a twisted way
of putting things.

458
00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:10.670
You don't seem to understand that you
are living proof of his savage blood.

459
00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:14.800
You run around spouting lies and use
violence when you don't get your way.

460
00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:18.630
To top it off, you cozy up to the lady
of the house to steal her fortune.

461
00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:22.640
– You're wrong! I only...
– Your father is a filthy, no-good pirate!

462
00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:24.470
Treachery is in your blood!

463
00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:26.390
Of course you would hatch
such an evil scheme!

464
00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:27.850
You won't let up, will you?!

465
00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:29.310
Stop it, Usopp! Please!

466
00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:30.600
[USOPP grunts]

467
00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:31.560
[KAYA] No more violence.

468
00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.440
I can't take it!

469
00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:37.070
Klahadore isn't a bad person...

470
00:21:37.070 --> 00:21:38.610
He's just...

471
00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:43.160
He's just trying to do what he thinks is best
for me and sometimes he goes too far.

472
00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:47.870
Leave this place.

473
00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:51.210
You are never
to come here again!

474
00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:53.040
Yeah, I get it.

475
00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:55.670
You don't have
to tell me twice, buddy.

476
00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:59.710
This is the last you'll
ever see of me.

477
00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:04.550
[KAYA whimpers] Usopp...

478
00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:04.220
[KIDS growling]

479
00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:06.180
Hey, you butler jerk!

480
00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:08.220
Our Captain's not
that kinda guy!

481
00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:09.600
Ya stupid jerk-face!

482
00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:12.890
Jerk-face!

483
00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:15.440
Shut up. You don't have
a bone to pick with him.

484
00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:16.520
[KLAHADORE growls]

485
00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:23.150
Put me down! Put me down!
I'm going to kick his ass!

486
00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:25.910
[KLAHADORE] You will
all leave immediately!

487
00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:39.380
Your meal is
ready now, Miss Kaya.

488
00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:42.260
[KAYA] No thank you,
I don't want it.

489
00:22:44.430 --> 00:22:46.430
[KLAHADORE sighs]

490
00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:50.350
The cook would be most
upset to hear you say that.

491
00:22:50.350 --> 00:22:52.730
He works his hardest,
day and night, to come up

492
00:22:52.730 --> 00:22:55.150
with delicious meals
that suit your needs.

493
00:22:55.150 --> 00:22:57.110
[silverware clinks]

494
00:22:57.110 --> 00:22:57.900
[KAYA gasps]

495
00:23:00.820 --> 00:23:03.070
[KAYA] Why were you
so cruel to him?

496
00:23:03.070 --> 00:23:06.110
I know I was wrong to talk
to Usopp without telling you.

497
00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:10.200
I will admit that much, and I'm very
sorry for not being honest with you,

498
00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:13.160
but this situation did not warrant
that kind of harsh treatment.

499
00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:18.840
May I sit down?

500
00:23:18.840 --> 00:23:20.340
[KAYA] Go ahead.

501
00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:25.470
[KLAHADORE] It has been quite some time
since I first arrived at this house.

502
00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:29.970
Soon it will be three years that I have
been in the service of your family.

503
00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:34.270
I will never forget what happened when
I showed up at your father's door.

504
00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:39.310
[KAYA gasps]

505
00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:46.200
[KLAHADORE] My former employers
were brutal, pitiless men.

506
00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:49.700
I'd been kicked off the ship I worked
on for some small blunder I had made.

507
00:23:49.700 --> 00:23:53.700
And with no work or money, I was
on the verge of dying like a beggar.

508
00:24:07.930 --> 00:24:11.220
[KLAHADORE] As far as I know, I
would've died without your father's help.

509
00:24:11.220 --> 00:24:13.430
I owe my life to your parents.

510
00:24:13.430 --> 00:24:18.310
And now that they're gone,
I owe my life to you.

511
00:24:19.150 --> 00:24:22.650
[KLAHADORE] I know that it isn't my place
to interfere with your friendships.

512
00:24:22.650 --> 00:24:24.610
I wouldn't have taken
such a bold step

513
00:24:25.280 --> 00:24:28.240
unless I thought
it absolutely necessary.

514
00:24:28.240 --> 00:24:33.280
It's just that Usopp isn't exactly known
for his upstanding character.

515
00:24:33.280 --> 00:24:36.250
You see, if anything were
to happen to you,

516
00:24:36.250 --> 00:24:38.460
it would be my fault
for not seeing to your safety

517
00:24:38.460 --> 00:24:42.250
and I would never be able to ask
forgiveness from your parents!

518
00:24:42.250 --> 00:24:46.460
Do you think ill of me
for my childish behavior earlier today?

519
00:24:46.460 --> 00:24:48.840
No, of course I don't.

520
00:24:48.840 --> 00:24:53.390
I'm thankful to have you around too,
Klahadore, but I stand by my opinion.

521
00:24:54.220 --> 00:24:56.680
Usopp is one of the
nicest people I know.

522
00:24:56.680 --> 00:24:58.310
[KLAHADORE] We'll see
about that.

523
00:24:58.310 --> 00:25:00.270
Until then, he is still
not welcome here.

524
00:25:01.600 --> 00:25:03.310
Klahadore! You blockhead!

525
00:25:03.310 --> 00:25:05.150
[KLAHADORE] "Blockhead"
will do just fine.

526
00:25:09.360 --> 00:25:10.660
[NAMI] Hey,
Where'd Luffy go?

527
00:25:12.280 --> 00:25:14.580
Who knows? He probably ran
after that captain.

528
00:25:15.160 --> 00:25:16.830
I bet he's at his secret spot!

529
00:25:16.830 --> 00:25:18.540
Yeah, over by the shore.

530
00:25:18.540 --> 00:25:21.540
He always goes there
when he's gonna think something over.

531
00:25:21.540 --> 00:25:24.630
[NAMI] Luffy can take care of himself,
but where's your other friend?

532
00:25:24.630 --> 00:25:26.500
[PEPPER, CARROT]
Oh yeah, Onion!

533
00:25:26.500 --> 00:25:29.510
Come to think of it, he just up
and disappears a lot.

534
00:25:29.510 --> 00:25:32.840
Yeah! And then he shows up
outta nowhere all freaked out!

535
00:25:32.840 --> 00:25:36.310
[ONION screaming] Terrible news, guys!

536
00:25:36.310 --> 00:25:37.680
You see?

537
00:25:37.680 --> 00:25:40.140
[ONION] Listen to me!

538
00:25:40.140 --> 00:25:43.270
Some nut job is on his way here
and he only walks backwards!

539
00:25:43.270 --> 00:25:44.230
[PEPPER, CARROT] You liar.

540
00:25:44.230 --> 00:25:46.360
It's the truth!

541
00:25:46.360 --> 00:25:47.610
There he is!

542
00:25:47.610 --> 00:25:48.650
[NAMI, PEPPER, CARROT] Hm?

543
00:25:56.620 --> 00:25:59.580
Now, which one of you people
has the nerve to call me weird?

544
00:25:59.620 --> 00:26:04.630
<b>Jango
A Hypnotist</b>

545
00:26:02.830 --> 00:26:05.710
I'm just a normal guy.

546
00:26:05.710 --> 00:26:07.840
S'that so? You look insane.

547
00:26:07.840 --> 00:26:09.170
[JANGO] Don't be silly.

548
00:26:09.170 --> 00:26:11.550
I'm just an ordinary, run
of the mill hypnotist.

549
00:26:11.550 --> 00:26:14.180
[ONION] A hypnotist?
Really? Awesome!

550
00:26:14.180 --> 00:26:15.800
[PEPPER] Show
us something!

551
00:26:15.800 --> 00:26:17.430
[CARROT] Yeah!
Do something!

552
00:26:18.470 --> 00:26:20.270
What?!

553
00:26:20.270 --> 00:26:23.350
You fools, what makes you think
that I would want to reveal

554
00:26:23.350 --> 00:26:27.190
my masterful hypnosis techniques
to a bunch of roadside strangers?

555
00:26:27.190 --> 00:26:28.690
[JANGO] Okay,
you convinced me.

556
00:26:28.690 --> 00:26:30.280
Now, watch the ring closely.

557
00:26:30.280 --> 00:26:31.320
[ZORO] What a ham!

558
00:26:31.320 --> 00:26:34.740
So, by the count of "Jango,"
you'll be in a deep sleep.

559
00:26:34.740 --> 00:26:35.950
Alright, are you ready?

560
00:26:35.950 --> 00:26:37.080
[KIDS gasping]

561
00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:38.080
[JANGO] One...

562
00:26:38.080 --> 00:26:39.200
Two...

563
00:26:39.200 --> 00:26:39.870
Jango!

564
00:26:41.500 --> 00:26:43.750
[KIDS, JANGO snoring]

565
00:26:43.750 --> 00:26:45.880
[ZORO] Who is
this freaky weirdo?!

566
00:26:50.340 --> 00:26:51.340
[LUFFY] Hi!

567
00:26:52.670 --> 00:26:53.800
What're you doin' here?

568
00:26:53.800 --> 00:26:57.100
[USOPP] I came here to be alone,
but I guess that's not happening!

569
00:26:57.100 --> 00:26:59.180
Did you follow me?
What d'you want?

570
00:26:59.180 --> 00:27:01.270
[LUFFY] Oh, ya know, nothin.

571
00:27:04.640 --> 00:27:06.480
[LUFFY] Oh...
Ouch... [laughs]

572
00:27:12.570 --> 00:27:14.450
[USOPP] I can't believe
that butler!

573
00:27:14.450 --> 00:27:16.660
Insulting my old man like that!

574
00:27:16.660 --> 00:27:19.280
[LUFFY] Yeah, I hate
that guy too!

575
00:27:19.280 --> 00:27:22.580
No matter what anyone says,
Yasopp was a great pirate.

576
00:27:22.580 --> 00:27:23.710
Yeah! Really!

577
00:27:23.710 --> 00:27:26.460
I've always looked up
to my old man for living every day

578
00:27:26.460 --> 00:27:29.000
with his life on the line,
out in the open ocean.

579
00:27:29.000 --> 00:27:31.710
He made a brave choice
and I admire him for that!

580
00:27:31.710 --> 00:27:35.260
And then that stupid, snotty butler
stomped all over my pride.

581
00:27:35.260 --> 00:27:36.890
He's gonna pay for this!

582
00:27:36.890 --> 00:27:38.010
Hey, wait.

583
00:27:38.010 --> 00:27:40.310
Do you know if you're ever
gonna see that girl again?

584
00:27:40.310 --> 00:27:44.100
[USOPP gasps] I
don't know. Eh...

585
00:27:44.100 --> 00:27:47.980
I'll consider it if that butler
apologizes to me for the things he said.

586
00:27:47.980 --> 00:27:49.400
That butler right there?

587
00:27:49.400 --> 00:27:55.110
Yeah... That's the one, if he... What
in the world is he doing down here?!

588
00:27:55.110 --> 00:27:57.320
[LUFFY] What's the big idea?

589
00:27:57.320 --> 00:27:58.450
Hey, Jango.

590
00:27:58.450 --> 00:28:01.950
I specifically ordered you
to keep yourself inconspicuous.

591
00:28:01.950 --> 00:28:04.250
That doesn't mean
sleeping in the road.

592
00:28:04.250 --> 00:28:08.040
Relax man, I've perfected
the skills of the chameleon.

593
00:28:08.040 --> 00:28:09.080
I blend in.

594
00:28:09.080 --> 00:28:11.920
[LUFFY] There's someone else
with him and, man, is he weird!

595
00:28:11.920 --> 00:28:13.300
I've never seen him before.

596
00:28:13.300 --> 00:28:14.840
Who is he?

597
00:28:14.840 --> 00:28:19.050
So, have all the necessary
preparations been made?

598
00:28:19.050 --> 00:28:20.720
But of course.

599
00:28:24.100 --> 00:28:29.100
[JANGO] We can start anytime...
on the "Rich Girl Murder Plan!"

600
00:28:29.100 --> 00:28:31.900
[LUFFY, USOPP gasp]

601
00:28:32.280 --> 00:28:33.680
[USOPP]
Murder?

602
00:28:41.530 --> 00:28:48.390
As a kid I had a dream of a dazzling treasure

603
00:28:48.590 --> 00:28:55.410
I had a map in my head that I knew would lead me

604
00:28:55.660 --> 00:29:02.510
Charted a course all on my own so nobody would beat me

605
00:29:02.630 --> 00:29:09.770
The promised land was in my hand drew a line in the sand

606
00:29:12.470 --> 00:29:15.150
Look where I am

607
00:29:17.380 --> 00:29:23.560
My one ambitions slipping right through my hands

608
00:29:23.900 --> 00:29:30.830
But if the world ever changes Ill call out your name

609
00:29:30.990 --> 00:29:37.910
We could return to a time when our lives were still the same

610
00:29:38.040 --> 00:29:45.040
Take me to the place where memories remain

611
00:29:45.140 --> 00:29:50.910
Please dont ever let them fade
